---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="System" description="Darshan Kansara's progression from physical infrastructure and datacenter operations to cloud, data platforms, and AI-enabled operations.">
  <header class="route-hero">
    <p class="route-code">System / 1998 → now</p>
    <div><h1>The abstractions changed.<br /><em>The responsibility did not.</em></h1><p>Servers became services. Datacenters became cloud regions. Platforms became operating systems for the business. Each layer widened the view without erasing the one beneath it.</p></div>
  </header>

  <nav class="era-index" aria-label="Career chapters"><a href="#now"><span>Now</span>Data platform</a><a href="#improvement"><span>2020</span>Cloud operations</a><a href="#cloud"><span>2011</span>Datacenter + cloud</a><a href="#service"><span>2005</span>Service delivery</a><a href="#foundation"><span>1998</span>Infrastructure</a></nav>

  <div class="career-record">
    <section id="now" class="chapter current">
      <aside><span>2022—Today</span><strong>Microsoft</strong><small>Layer 05</small></aside>
      <div class="chapter-body"><p class="role">Senior Manager · Platform Reliability &amp; Operations</p><h2>Operate the data platform as a product.</h2><p>Leading reliability, security, infrastructure, continuity, and cost discipline for a business-critical cloud marketing data platform built on Azure services including Synapse, Cosmos DB, and Fabric.</p><blockquote>Can engineering, privacy, security, compliance, and operations see the same system?</blockquote><dl><div><dt>Economics</dt><dd>$1M+ annual platform spend reduction through capacity optimization, automation, and removal of recurring inefficiency.</dd></div><div><dt>Signals</dt><dd>Clearer monitoring, incident response, and readiness practices across the platform.</dd></div><div><dt>Current edge</dt><dd>Telemetry, runbook context, and cost signals shaped into bounded operational assistance.</dd></div></dl></div>
    </section>

    <section id="improvement" class="chapter">
      <aside><span>2020—2022</span><strong>Microsoft</strong><small>Layer 04</small></aside>
      <div class="chapter-body"><p class="role">Senior Program Manager · Cloud Operations &amp; Continuous Improvement</p><h2>Turn capacity pressure into an improvement system.</h2><p>Connected demand forecasting, spares planning, finance, and supply-chain decisions so cost and operational risk could appear earlier. Lean and Kaizen became tools for removing recurring delay, not presentation language.</p><blockquote>Where is pressure accumulating, and who can act before it becomes failure?</blockquote></div>
    </section>

    <section id="cloud" class="chapter">
      <aside><span>2011—2020</span><strong>Microsoft</strong><small>Layer 03</small></aside>
      <div class="chapter-body"><p class="role">Datacenter Strategy, Automation &amp; Reliability Leadership</p><h2>Move uncertainty out of production.</h2><p>Worked across Azure datacenter tooling, critical-environment IT, automation, and global operations as cloud scale accelerated. Established the first Azure Datacenter Instrumentation &amp; Pre-Production Lab so infrastructure changes could be tested before broad rollout.</p><blockquote>How can the system fail somewhere designed for learning first?</blockquote></div>
    </section>

    <section id="service" class="chapter">
      <aside><span>2005—2011</span><strong>TCS · Microsoft</strong><small>Layer 02</small></aside>
      <div class="chapter-body"><p class="role">Service Delivery &amp; IT Operations</p><h2>Learn consequence through customer-facing services.</h2><p>Owned service delivery and datacenter operations for Microsoft online services across India and Redmond. Availability, incident response, and service-level commitments made the relationship between technical choices and customer experience impossible to ignore.</p><blockquote>What does technical failure mean to the person waiting for the service?</blockquote></div>
    </section>

    <section id="foundation" class="chapter">
      <aside><span>1998—2005</span><strong>India</strong><small>Layer 01</small></aside>
      <div class="chapter-body"><p class="role">Infrastructure &amp; Networking</p><h2>The foundation was physical.</h2><p>Servers, networks, operating systems, and the hands-on work beneath the service. Proximity to the machine created an enduring preference: understand what the abstraction is hiding before deciding how to improve it.</p><blockquote>What is the machine actually doing?</blockquote></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="credentials"><p class="route-code">Formal foundation</p><div><h2>Credentials, kept in proportion.</h2><p>PMP · PMI-ACP · ITIL v3 · CDCP · CDCS</p><p>MCSE · CCNA · HP PSE · CNE</p><p>Post Graduate Diploma in Information Technology · Diploma in Computer Engineering</p></div></section>
  <section class="next"><p>The progression explains the method.</p><h2>The evidence shows whether it worked.</h2><div><a href="/impact">Open the evidence →</a><a href="/projects">See what I build →</a></div></section>

  <style>
    :global(body),:global(main){background:var(--ink);color:var(--text)}.route-code,.role,.chapter aside,.chapter dt{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.route-code{color:var(--gold)}
    .route-hero,.era-index,.career-record,.credentials,.next>*{width:min(var(--max),calc(100% - 2 * var(--pad)));margin-inline:auto}.route-hero{min-height:calc(78svh - 100px);padding-block:clamp(70px,9vw,118px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:var(--rail) 1fr;gap:var(--gutter);align-items:end;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.route-hero h1{max-width:17ch;color:var(--paper);font-size:clamp(3.2rem,5vw,5rem);font-weight:400;line-height:.98}.route-hero h1 em{color:var(--azure-bright);font-style:normal}.route-hero div>p{max-width:58ch;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.08rem}
    .era-index{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.era-index a{min-height:82px;padding:17px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--paper);font-size:.78rem}.era-index span{display:block;margin-bottom:5px;color:var(--gold);font: .58rem var(--font-mono)}
    .career-record{position:relative}.career-record::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:calc(var(--rail) + var(--gutter) - 1px);top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:linear-gradient(var(--gold),var(--azure),var(--line))}.chapter{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:var(--rail) 1fr;gap:var(--gutter);padding:clamp(64px,8vw,108px) 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.chapter::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:calc(var(--rail) + var(--gutter) - 4px);top:72px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--azure);box-shadow:0 0 0 6px var(--ink)}.chapter.current::before{background:var(--gold)}.chapter aside{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;color:var(--dim)}.chapter aside span{color:var(--gold)}.chapter aside small{margin-top:24px}.chapter-body{max-width:880px}.role{color:var(--azure-bright)}.chapter h2,.credentials h2,.next h2{color:var(--paper);font-size:clamp(2.2rem,3.8vw,3.65rem);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0}.chapter-body>p:not(.role){max-width:66ch;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.02rem}.chapter blockquote{margin:34px 0 0;padding-left:22px;border-left:2px solid var(--gold);color:var(--paper);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2vw,1.6rem)}.chapter dl{margin:42px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.chapter dl div{padding:20px 18px 0 0}.chapter dt{color:var(--gold)}.chapter dd{margin:8px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}
    .credentials{padding-block:var(--section);display:grid;grid-template-columns:var(--rail) 1fr;gap:var(--gutter)}.credentials>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:16px var(--gutter)}.credentials h2{grid-row:1/4}.credentials p{margin:0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.86rem}.next{padding-block:clamp(76px,9vw,118px);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.next>p{color:var(--gold);font: .62rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase}.next h2{max-width:18ch}.next>div{display:flex;gap:22px;margin-top:28px}.next a{color:var(--azure-bright)}
    @media(max-width:760px){.route-hero{min-height:auto;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.route-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,12vw,3.6rem)}.era-index{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.career-record::before{left:4px}.chapter{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding-left:24px}.chapter::before{left:1px}.chapter aside{flex-direction:row;flex-wrap:wrap}.chapter aside small{width:100%;margin-top:3px}.chapter dl{grid-template-columns:1fr}.credentials{grid-template-columns:1fr}.credentials>div{grid-template-columns:1fr}.credentials h2{grid-row:auto}.next>div{flex-direction:column}}
  </style>
</Base>
